    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0074" n="62" xml:id="pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860F.00/762: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Des
                            Portes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-03-26T12:00:00-05:00">March 26,
                            1939—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Your 8, March 24, 4 p.m. After thanking the Foreign Minister for his
                    confidence in consulting this Government with respect to the dismemberment of
                    Czechoslovakia you should give him copies of the statement issued by the Acting
                    Secretary on March 17, and a copy of the reply of this Government to the note
                    from the German Embassy, this reply being dated March 20 (see radio bulletin for
                    texts).</p>
                <p>Although, as is evident from the statement of the Acting Secretary, the
                    Department views with concern recent developments in Central Europe, it does not
                    believe that these developments present occasion for initiating the procedure of
                    consultation as provided for in the Buenos Aires Pact<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d59-f1"/> and the Declaration of Lima.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d59-f2"
                    /> The Foreign Minister’s suggestion will be borne in mind, however, for future
                    reference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
